sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: the run of the proof cases of one command (Nick + orchestrator, 2026-11-05), the "Run the proof" step of proof:run. The Gateway admits intent; Orbit's own Swamp runs the cases in batches over SSH; the Gateway projects the report once. Built as the workflow proof-fleet-verify and its batch and case children.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · started by proof:run
  %% kind: proof.verify
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane VM icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant VM as Proof task VM<br/>reached over ssh
  Note over GW: Admit the run<br/>owned task VM · one command
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the proof group is open and owns its task VM workspace
  %%> - the nested fleet of the VM was reset and has its `base` snapshot
  GW->>SW: Start one run<br/>proof-fleet-verify
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the cases file of the command, the checkout path, the group and the pinned SSH identity of the task VM
  %%> - no secret, and no step calls back to the Gateway
  SW->>VM: Select the cases<br/>runner plan --lines
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - one line a batch, `BATCH SETUP CASE...`, in the order of `swamp/proof/batches.yaml`; inside a batch, in file order
  VM-->>SW: Ordered plan<br/>batches · cases
  loop each batch, one at a time
    opt not the first batch
      SW->>VM: Restore base<br/>runner restore
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - the phase `base-restore`, one 45 s limit, no retry
      %%> - a restore that fails prints a failed line; the cases of the batch and every later batch become `unrun` with cause `infrastructure`, and the verdicts already reached stay
    end
    opt the batch declares a start state
      SW->>VM: Set up the batch<br/>runner setup
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - runs the setup steps of the batch; a setup that fails or is not built stops the run like a failed restore
    end
    loop each case, one at a time, one child workflow
      SW->>VM: Run one case<br/>runner case ID
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - the step allows failure, so a failed case does not stop its batch
      %%> Returns:
      %%> - one JSON line of at most 1 KB: the case id, the verdict, the cause, the seconds and the failed checks
      opt the case did not pass and is not the last of its batch
        SW->>VM: Restore base<br/>then the batch setup
        %%> Why:
        %%> - a failed case can leave anything behind; the next case starts clean
        %%> - the last case of a batch skips it, because the next batch restores anyway
      end
    end
    Note over SW: Join the batch lines<br/>report
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - a case that printed no line is `failed` with cause `infrastructure`; a case that did not run is `unrun` with cause `infrastructure`
  end
  Note over SW: Join the verdicts<br/>report
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - every case of the plan has one line, in plan order
  %%> - the Gateway reads this step once, when the run ends
  SW-->>GW: Native terminal result<br/>verdict lines
  Note over GW: Record the verdicts<br/>one row for each case
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the proof run reads the rows, resets the fleet for the next command, or cancels the group
  %%> - the workflow ends succeeded when it reports; whether a case passed is in its row, not in the status
